# The README exists three times

| File | Language | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `README.md` | English | Canonical — write here first |
| `README.pt-BR.md` | Português (Brasil) | Translation |
| `README.es.md` | Español | Translation |

**A change to one is a change to all three.** Editing only `README.md` leaves the project
shipping documentation that contradicts itself. Do not hand back a partial update.

## Rules

- Keep the same section order, heading structure and table rows in every file. A reader should
  be able to follow along across languages.
- Translate prose. Do **not** translate: code, commands, file paths, env var names, env var
  values, log strings, or model slugs.
- Table cells describing a variable get translated; the variable name and its default do not.
- Each file opens with the switcher line, current language in bold and unlinked:

  ```markdown
  **Read this in other languages:** **English** | [Português (Brasil)](README.pt-BR.md) | [Español](README.es.md)
  ```

  In `README.pt-BR.md` the lead-in is `**Leia em outros idiomas:**`, in `README.es.md` it is
  `**Léelo en otros idiomas:**`.
- Relative links resolve from the repository root in all three, so they are identical across
  files. Do not rewrite them per language.
- Adding a language means adding it to the switcher in every existing README.
